This is a proof-of-concept setup of White Rabbit which utilizes the Fractional PLLs on an AMD Ultrascale+ FPGA
according to XAPP1276. Only a commonly available ZCU102 board is needed, without any external PLLs. SFP2 is being used
for 1G ethernet IO and upstream connectivity. For more information, please have a look at the following slides:
https://indico.cern.ch/event/1379641/contributions/5863216/attachments/2824424/4933446/12_Light%20Rabbit.pdf
("Light Rabbit" at the 13th WR workshop and WR Collaboration Launch, Geneva (Switzerland), 2024)

To build a Vivado project and synthesize the bitstream follow these steps:

$ hdlmake # make sure to use a recent version of hdlmake, preferably straight from the repo and not pip
$ make files.tcl
$ vivado -mode tcl -source zcu102.tcl
